WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.998
The headline is a clean sweep.

00:00:04.078 --> 00:00:08.077
Across all three standard benchmarks and all six
high-resolution ImageNet subsets,

00:00:08.157 --> 00:00:12.155
SPEED sets new state-of-the-art.

00:00:12.235 --> 00:00:16.233
At the tightest one-image-per-class budget, it
reaches forty percent on CIFAR-100,

00:00:16.313 --> 00:00:20.312
a six point gain, and twenty-six point nine percent
on TinyImageNet,

00:00:20.392 --> 00:00:24.390
a ten point nine gain over the previous best.

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:28.468
On the ImageNet subsets it averages an eleven point
two percent improvement at the same budget.

00:00:28.548 --> 00:00:32.547
Strikingly,

00:00:32.627 --> 00:00:36.625
its one-image-per-class results match what prior
methods needed ten images per class to achieve,

00:00:36.705 --> 00:00:40.703
using only about ten percent of their storage.

00:00:40.783 --> 00:00:44.782
It also stays best at every step of continual learning,

00:00:44.862 --> 00:00:48.860
and under corruption on ResNet18 it nearly doubles
the accuracy of prior methods.
